    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d649">

                <pb facs="0775" n="1609" xml:id="pg1609"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 654.119/238a</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in France</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Sharp</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-04-11">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 11, 1918</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3515. For McFadden [from War Trade Board]:</p>
                <p>No. 29. We have cabled Dresel our opinion that negotiations with Switzerland for
                    lumber and other commodities should be conducted at Berne rather than at Paris.
                    Will you please be guided accordingly.</p>
                <p> Dresel suggests that inter-Ally commission on lumber should go from Paris to
                    Berne and should include American representative. We approve of this
                    suggestion.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
